From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:11:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [playback-manager] Don't un-mute the microphone when muting
 the speaker.

setMuteSpeaker() sent the playback manager's RequestMute with the
inverted flag. RequestMute is the microphone mute, as setMuteMicrophone()
uses it, so muting the speaker un-muted the microphone and un-muting
the speaker muted it, while the manager kept reporting the old
microphone state. The playback manager has no speaker mute, so don't
send anything for it.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 .../playback-manager/src/playbackmanagerplugin.cpp | 14 ++++----------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plugins/playback-manager/src/playbackmanagerplugin.cpp b/plugins/playback-manager/src/playbackmanagerplugin.cpp
index db09949..398e09f 100644
--- a/plugins/playback-manager/src/playbackmanagerplugin.cpp
+++ b/plugins/playback-manager/src/playbackmanagerplugin.cpp
@@ -158,16 +158,10 @@ void PlaybackManagerPlugin::setMuteSpeaker(bool on)
 {
     TRACE
     Q_D(PlaybackManagerPlugin);
-    QDBusMessage message = QDBusMessage::createMethodCall(ORG_MAEMO_PLAYBACK_DEST,
-                                                          ORG_MAEMO_PLAYBACK_PATH,
-                                                          ORG_MAEMO_PLAYBACK_IFACE,
-                                                          ORG_MAEMO_PLAYBACK_REQUEST_MUTE);
-    message << !on;
-
-    if (!QDBusConnection::sessionBus().send(message)) {
-        WARNING_T("Failed to send RequestMute method call.");
-        return;
-    }
+    // The playback manager has no speaker mute. RequestMute is the
+    // microphone mute (see setMuteMicrophone()), so sending it here, as this
+    // used to, un-muted the microphone whenever the speaker was muted.
+    DEBUG_T("Speaker mute %s is not supported by the playback manager.", on ? "on" : "off");
 
     d->manager->onMuteSpeakerChanged(on);
 }
